      "title": "Letterboxd review of Black Widow",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Black Widow\"] This feels quite old-fashioned, albeit in the best way possible. Many of the scenes are very stagey (I still can't quite believe it wasn't based on a play), most of the characters are two-dimensional types (the mouthy, unreliable wife; the husband who isn't as honest as he seems; the cop who is a little more clever than everyone gives him credit for), and it's set against a backdrop of New York theater, a reality which makes it impossible not to think of All About Eve as the story kicks into gear.But it's so much fun! Yes, the characters are two-dimensional, but how much does it really matter",
